    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer planar dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Materials: Ta2O5 (high index) and SiO2 (low index), alternating starting with Ta2O5. Initialize all Ta2O5 layers at quarter-wave optical thickness for 1550 nm (approximately 157 nm physical thickness assuming n≈2.45), all SiO2 layers at quarter-wave optical thickness for 1550 nm (approximately 267 nm assuming n≈1.46). Apply optimization bounds of ±4 nm around these quarter-wave targets. Add hard penalty constraint on adjacent-layer thickness gradients: |t_i - t_{i+1}| ≤ 12 nm for all adjacent pairs. Add lightweight stochastic offsets ≤2 nm to preserve asymmetry. Optimize for maximum transmittance at 1550 nm (single wavelength), minimum mean transmittance across 1400-1500 nm band, minimum mean transmittance across 1600-1700 nm band. Total layer count fixed at 20. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with these constraints. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
